cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use edgar-eval or S-1 Bench, please cite it as below."
title: "edgar-eval: S-1 Bench and skills for verifiable AI analysis of SEC filings"
abstract: >-
  Two agent skills and a benchmark for verifiable AI analysis of SEC filings. filing-factsheet
  builds a compact, page-cited fact sheet from a filing's HTML tables so a small open model can
  answer financial questions, with arithmetic and answer checks done in code. filing-evals builds,
  validates, and scores quote-anchored question sets with code-based checks including quote
  grounding, and guards against circularity with ablations and held-out filings. S-1 Bench has 47
  questions over Anthropic, PBC's Form S-1, plus a dev set (Reddit) and held-out sets (Klaviyo,
  Instacart) written after the pipeline was frozen.
type: software
authors:
